  "analytical_usefulness": 0.88,
  "source_groundedness": 0.8,
  "rationale": "The added columns decompose food quality into genuinely distinct, query-relevant facets (taste, texture, freshness, smell, appearance, ingredients, packaging, consistency/brand) plus a primary-facet roll-up, giving strong analytical leverage for 'what aspects reviewers focus on' with real grouping and comparison power. None are near-constant restatements of original columns. Grounding is generally sound with correct silence handling, but several flags are loose or overextended (packaging_quantity flagged from price/delivery mentions, ingredients_nutrition stretched to include flavor/nuts, and a missed explicit 'smells better' signal), which mildly depresses groundedness. Judged only on usefulness and groundedness, the set passes both necessary conditions."
